Article 34

1. In order to ensure the effectiveness of the implementation of KLA development policies in the Region, a KLA Task Force shall be established.
(2) The KLA Task Force as referred to in paragraph (1) shall have the main tasks, namely:
a. coordinating the implementation of KLA policies and development;
b. determining the tasks of KLA Task Force members;
c. conducting socialization, advocacy, and communication of information and education on KLA policies;
d. collecting baseline data;
e. conducting needs analysis sourced from baseline data;
f. disseminating baseline data;
g. determining the focus and priorities of programs in realizing KLA, which are adjusted to the potential of the Region;
h. preparing a regional action plan and KLA working mechanism for 5 (five) years; and
i. conducting monitoring, evaluation, and reporting at least once (1) a year.
3. Further provisions regarding the procedures for appointment and dismissal of KLA Task Force membership shall be regulated by Regent Regulation.

