a. the right to respect for survival, growth and development;
b. the right to basic services;
c. the right to equal protection;
d. the right to be free from various stigma; and/or
e. the right to obtain freedom.
2. In the case of a Child as a perpetrator of sexual violence or a criminal offender, the child has the right to obtain legal assistance and other assistance as well as to obtain special handling related to the confidentiality of their identity.

